# Scene 1: Room 12. Mme Kchaou with a clipboard; Nour sits at the desk by the door.
# Check vote.

~ start
Mme Kchaou: Desks spaced. Seating plan posted. Room number on the door. Every written rule, met.
Nour: Excuse me... the clock is behind us. And I have extra time. When everyone leaves after two hours, the door bangs every thirty seconds.
Mme Kchaou: The rules say nothing about clocks or doors.
do Story.show_card(2)
Room 12 meets every written rule, yet a candidate can't work in it. Which part of quality fails?
- Fitness for use\: a candidate can't use it as intended.
	do GameState.record_vote(1, "A")
	do GameState.fairness += 15
	do GameState.set_flag("room12_fixed")
	You move the clock to the front and give Nour the quiet desk at the back.
	Mme Kchaou: Hm. The rules didn't ask for that. (Writes something down.) Good.
- Conformance to requirements\: the room breaks the specification.
	do GameState.record_vote(1, "B")
	=> wrong
- Neither\: it meets every written rule, so it passes.
	do GameState.record_vote(1, "C")
	=> wrong
=> END

~ wrong
do GameState.fairness -= 5
Nour: It meets the rules. It still doesn't work for me.
Mme Kchaou: Conforming is not the same as being fit for use. The candidate is the customer here.
do Story.show_card(2)
do GameState.set_flag("room12_fixed")
You fix the room anyway.
=> END
